# Reproduction for bd inc-a7jq, scenario C: the control. The drops here are NOT
# from a kill by the player's party: the victim dies to the wizard-mode
# "Genocide Everything", which is the victim's own death with no killer. A
# non-hostile human must still take them. Read by tools/check_loot_claim.sh.
# This is the same arrangement as scenario A, so a difference between the two
# is the kill and nothing else.

@dump:arrival
w
y
@choose "Genocide Everything"
w
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*10 SPACE           # Freeze Monsters ON (row 11)
@dump:freeze-on
ESC

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Kobolds"
@choose "kobold"
LEFT ENTER              # the victim, adjacent west

w
@choose "Genocide Everything"   # the kobold dies with no killer; its drops fall

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Humans"
@choose "human"
LEFT*2 ENTER            # the non-hostile creature, two squares west
@dump:killed

w
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*10 SPACE           # Freeze Monsters OFF
@dump:freeze-off
ESC
.*10                    # ten turns, the player in the room and in view
@dump:waited
v
@dump:log
ESC
@quit
